{"title":"Divisibility rules/Rule 2 for 13 proof","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_2_for_13_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This is based on <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_for_11_proof\" title=\"Divisibility rules/Rule for 11 proof\"> divisibility by 11 rule </a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_1_for_7_proof\" title=\"Divisibility rules/Rule 1 for 7 proof\"> divisibility by 7 rule </a></i>\n</p><p>Assume N has 3k digits, otherwise add zeros to the left.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\"> WLOG </a> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e753caa85cb6565afb12e08a24b8d780e175e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}\\cdots a_8a_7a_6a_5a_4a_3a_2a_1a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"348\" height=\"18\" /> where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_numbers\" title=\"Base numbers\"> base-ten</a> numbers. \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6061fb91f5554bf80da7bf10ee346eaf42e6f7e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 10^{3k-1} a_{3k-1} + 10^{3k-2} a_{3k-2} + 10^{3k-3} a_{3k-3} \\cdots + 10^8 a_8 + 10^7 a_7 + 10^6 a_6 + 10^5 a_5 + 10^4 a_4 + 10^3 a_3 + 10^2 a_2 + 10 a_1 + a_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"942\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/55600bf93e225802cf139a5e15c339156372e066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 1000^{k-1} (100 a_{3k-1} + 10 a_{3k-2} + a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + 1000^2 (100 a_8 + 10 a_7 + a_6) + 1000 (100 a_5 + 10 a_4 + a_3) + (100 a_2 + 10 a_1 + a_0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"953\" height=\"22\" />\nRewriting as 3 digit numbers, that is, partitioning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> into 3 digit numbers (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7b7175fba3442d3f6735d1811c22c94ea94745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}\\cdots a_8a_7a_6 a_5a_4a_3 a_2a_1a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"307\" height=\"14\" />).\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282ad3e5eba8ef1a81ce55cd527129776570d604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 1000^{k-1} (a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + 1000^2 (a_8a_7a_6) + 1000 (a_5a_4a_3) + (a_2a_1a_0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"593\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f8111ffd9b88f059e4d433f61704624b4f4ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000\\equiv -1\\pmod{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d384c3c2a6dbd0cd6a064a468b456ae53e03ac15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000^{k-1} (a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + 1000^2 (a_8a_7a_6) + 1000 (a_5a_4a_3) + (a_2a_1a_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"569\" height=\"22\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19e35061422a2eb4ad96d895eee4008418bd833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv (-1)^{k-1} (a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + (-1)^2 (a_8a_7a_6) - (a_5a_4a_3) + (a_2a_1a_0) \\pmod {13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"640\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>This is the alternating sum of groups of 3 digit numbers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, which is what we wanted.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_2_for_13_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules\" title=\"Divisibility rules\"> Back to divisibility rules</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 64/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2655/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25896:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082945 and revision id 205704. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}